# DEP-006 — keep secrets and build noise out of the image and its layers.
#
# Owner: Member 6 (Testing + Benchmarking + Docker + Deployment)
#
# Anything listed here never enters the build context, so it cannot end up in a
# layer even transiently — which matters, because a file deleted in a later
# RUN is still present in the layer that added it and still readable via
# `docker history` / layer extraction.
#
# Acceptance (DEP-006): `docker history` on the built image shows no secret
# values. Verify with `python -m scripts.verify_container --check-secrets`.

# ---- Secrets: never build these in ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*_rsa
credentials.json
secrets/

# ---- Version control and CI ----
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ---- Local Python environments and caches ----
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- Tests, benchmarks and notebooks: not runtime code ----
tests/
benchmark/
notebooks/
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- Data: the corpus is mounted or ingested, not baked in ----
# Keeping data/ out matters for size (embeddings.json alone is ~3 MB) and for
# provenance: an image with a stale copy of the corpus grades against data
# nobody can trace. Populate the store via scripts/build_vector_store.py against
# the mounted volume instead.
data/
Database/
chroma_data/

# ---- Local artifacts ----
logs/
*.log
artifacts/
outputs/
tmp/
temp/

# ---- Editor and OS noise ----
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Docs: useful in the repo, dead weight in the image ----
docs/
*.md
!README.md
